ey-numbers-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":10,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"772bea6adab050ea03034e09097b6d109062f7ac2120c22ae7a2d403c0166b2c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Cycle-clique-Ramsey-numbers-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c8e8d7bf3c507b4a016a208d8f2484b04c677f5cd23f99f86304a4b97b4be967","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Cycle-clique-Ramsey-numbers-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L10"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor all integers $m\\ge n\\ge3$ with $(m,n)\\ne(3,3)$,\n\\[\n R(C_m,K_n)=(m-1)(n-1)+1.\n\\]\nFor the excluded pair, $R(C_3,K_3)=6$."}
